{
  "title": "Indian economy expanded by 8.4% in final three months of 2023",
  "publication_date": "2024-03-01T00:00:00Z",
  "summary": "India's economy showed remarkable growth in Q4 2023, with GDP rising 8.4% year-over-year, driven primarily by strong manufacturing performance according to official government data.",
  "content": "A boom in manufacturing helped propel India's economy to significant growth in the October to December quarter of 2023, with annual GDP expanding 8.4% compared to the same period in 2022, according to official government figures.\n\nThe impressive growth rate underscores India's position as one of the world's fastest-growing major economies, outpacing other large nations. Manufacturing played a key role in this expansion, demonstrating the country's increasing industrial capacity.\n\nThe GDP figures exceeded most economists' expectations and suggest strong domestic demand and industrial activity despite global economic headwinds.",
