  "markdown_content": "## Economic Performance\\n\\nManufacturing boom propelled India's economy to significant growth in the October to December quarter of 2023, with annual GDP expanding 8.4% compared to the same period in 2022, according to official government figures.\\n\\nThe impressive growth rate underscores India's position as one of the world's fastest-growing major economies, outpacing other large nations. Manufacturing played a key role in this expansion, demonstrating the country's increasing industrial capacity.\\n\\nThe GDP figures exceeded most economists' expectations and suggest strong domestic demand and industrial activity despite global economic headwinds.",
